cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Rocky planets in the habitable zone: code and data for a dated census of the NASA Exoplanet Archive"
type: software
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/payam-asa/exoplanet-hz-census"
authors:
  - family-names: Asadinia
    given-names: Payam
    affiliation: "Learn Satit Pattana School, Bangkok, Thailand"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3953-6104"
abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebook and data that select rocky (R <= 1.6 Earth radii) planets in
  the Kopparapu et al. (2014) habitable zone from the NASA Exoplanet Archive
  Planetary Systems Composite Parameters table (pscomppars, downloaded
  22 November 2026), rank them by the Earth Similarity Index, and flag whether
  each radius was measured by transit or estimated from a mass-radius relation.
  Includes the archive snapshot, the ranked table of 32 planets and the
  habitable-zone figure.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - habitable zone
  - Earth Similarity Index
  - NASA Exoplanet Archive
  - rocky planets
  - reproducibility
